{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1017301-novas-in-the-seventies","id":1017301,"title":"Novas in the seventies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T14:03:25-08:00","id":1017301,"title":"Novas in the seventies","content":"In the original Trinity timeline, there was a reference to superheroes first appearing in 1970, 28 years before N-Day. This reference was subsequently excised from all later versions of the timeline. Does anyone know anything about this, or has anyone tried to use it in a game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:53:51-08:00","id":1017333,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the 70's reference was written before Aberrant was written, and represents an alternate idea they didn't go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:00:47-08:00","id":1017575,"title":"","content":"I think there is a newspaper article clipping in one of the books about a man stopping a train or moving his car off the tracks with suspected mega-strength in the 50's but a breif scan of the books where i thought that was didn't turn anything up. Not much is said about it, but there are also some records about a tiny N-day burst sometime in the seventies - that Divis Mal might have caused. I'm not certain, but i believe it suffered the Adventure! curse of being fairly well documented but taken as nonsense by the greater scientific community who simply dismissed the event due to lack of evidence.<br /> -shrug-<br /> My brother used those novas in his settings, in fact my brother thinks that stalwarts, mesmers and talents continued to erupt in the intervening years after Adventure! I remember he took a great deal of inspiration from capcom fighting games and a tv from the mid eighties. I thought it was a bit silly to start with, but the whole game was full of fun silver-age sequences and he was more than capable of reconstucting the ideas. I'm sure that isn't the only way to use this obscure nova lore, but it's a way i've seen done with success.<br /> I tried to get you some page references, but apart from the section in the A:PG, i'm a bit rusty on where to look for things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:17:24-08:00","id":1017581,"title":"","content":"The article you're thinking about is from Project Utopia, and is dated 1964. Thanks for the help. Can't wait for Trinity Continuum!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:37:03-08:00","id":1017590,"title":"","content":"Ah, very astute of you - that sounds like it, if your Signature is true i wish you great luck in your history - any questions about the Trinity universe of old will be welcome here. I'm not sure continuum is going to be very condusive to linear history - since history may be at the player's fingertips. But, i always had a fondness for the old meta-plot, desite the obstacles it would sometimes erect against good storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:57:34-08:00","id":1189080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1017301-novas-in-the-seventies#post1017301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original Trinity timeline, there was a reference to superheroes first appearing in 1970, 28 years before N-Day. This reference was subsequently excised from all later versions of the timeline. Does anyone know anything about this, or has anyone tried to use it in a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was also mention of this in the Aberrant Players Guide. That Novas have been around down through history, but were low powered (10-20 nova points). <br /> <br /> This made me ponder a team of Cold War Novas fighting atomic threats for the government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}